<file path="README.md">
# Solvra redesign — drop-in overlay

Design implemented: `claude_inspired_minimalist_ai_workspace` (warm paper + terracotta).
Behaviour, API contract (`/api/chat`), data model and the `chatbot_conversations`
localStorage key are unchanged — existing chats keep working.

## Apply

1. Copy these folders over your project root (merge; `app/page.tsx` is replaced):
   `app/`  `lib/`  `public/`
   Do NOT touch `app/api/chat/route.ts` or `.env.local`.

2. Install dependencies (fonts are self-hosted, so no Google Fonts / offline build issues):

   npm i react-markdown remark-gfm lucide-react \
     @fontsource-variable/inter @fontsource-variable/newsreader \
     @fontsource/instrument-serif @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono

3. `npm run dev`

## Notes
- Product name lives in `lib/brand.ts` (`APP_NAME`). The design mock says "Sovra",
  your logo file is `solvra.jpg` — set whichever is correct.
- `page.tsx` is now a thin client-only shell; all state/streaming logic is in
  `app/components/ChatApp.tsx`.
- `ChatMessage` gained an optional `error?: boolean` (failed turns are shown in
  the chat but never sent back to the model).
</file>

</files>
